From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jose Zamora Cifras <44040559+JoseZamoraCifras@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:51:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fs: saves named before backslash paths are copied to their
 new names at mount

Builds before 7c23cc0 (backslashes separate path components, PR #513) took a
backslash as part of a name, so a game that opens save:\savedata0.bin stored a
file named "\savedata0.bin". Since that change the host looks for
savedata0.bin, finds nothing, and the save looks lost: The Legend of Zelda:
Link's Awakening (01006BB00C6F0000) shows every file of its file select as
"New game" while the old files are still in the save folder.

At each transactional save mount, right after the work directory is cloned,
save_legacy_names clones each entry whose guest name has a backslash (a file,
or a directory with its tree) to the path that name names now, makes its
parent directories by exact guest name (a case collision gets an alias, as a
create does), and marks the old entry with an attribute so that this happens
once: a copy the game erases later stays erased. It never overwrites an entry
and keeps the old one, which a build before the change still reads. One log
line per copy; a name that leads above the save's root, or a copy the disk
refuses, logs a red line and is tried again at the next mount.

It works in the work directory only, so it rides the save transaction: the
copies reach the committed save with the game's own Commit, and a kill or a
remount before that leaves the committed save as it was and does the same
again. A lookup that falls back to the old name would have had to teach every
write, create, rename, delete and listing about it, and an erased file would
have come back.

Test: dm/host/tests/t_fs_backslash.c (make -C dm/host/tests fs-backslash).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: games that write save:\name paths (Link's Awakening) keep the saves builds before upstream 7c23cc0 stored under backslash names
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#461

